==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} ''[[bleh]]'', from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} ''[[*bligh]]'', "gleaming"; related to ''[[bleich]]'', ''[[Blitz]]'', ''[[Blick]]'', ''[[blecken]]'', ''[[blank]]'', ''[[blinken]]'', ''[[blinzeln]]'', ''[[blaken]]''

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɛç|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n||gen2=Bleches|Bleche}}

# [[sheet]] (out of metal)
# {{context|informal|music|lang=de}} [[brass|Brass]], a collective term for all brass instruments, or all brass players, etc.
#: {{usex|„Das '''Blech''' spielt bitte mal alleine!“ rief der Dirigent.|The conductor demanded loudly: “Brass play on their own now, please!”|lang=de}}

